  "mechanismSummary": "The alcohol (here cyclohexanol) is first made into its S-methyl xanthate with NaH, CS₂ and MeI. The tin radical adds to the C=S sulfur, giving a stabilised carbon radical. This fragments (β-scission): the C–O bond to the alcohol carbon breaks as a strong C=O forms, releasing the cyclohexyl radical. It takes H from Bu₃SnH, giving cyclohexane and a new Bu₃Sn•. Overall an alcohol is reduced to an alkane, which no polar reagent does directly.",
